  "summary": "dnspython dns.name.from_wire_parser() excessive CPU use",
  "details": "### Impact\nA maliciously crafted DNS message may cause dns.name.from_wire_parser() to use excessive CPU for DNS name decompression.  Applications that process untrusted DNS wire form messages with dnspython may be degraded or DoS'd by the extra CPU use required.\n\n### Patches\nThis problem is fixed in dnspython 2.9.0.\n\n### Workarounds\nThere are no known workarounds.\n\n### Credit\nEvgenios Gkritsis, Department of Informatics, University of Piraeus \u0026 Athena Research Center, Greece\nConstantinos Patsakis, Department of Informatics, University of Piraeus \u0026 Athena Research Center, Greece\nGeorge Stergiopoulos, Department of Informatics, Athens University of Economics and Business, Greece",
